{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/user.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372607Z","id":"94ab5cdaf4de5bbed63a3fac96b1c4d50f4102b26fc9a41c5430dbdc8a8c63ea","body":{"detail":"The header says Clax has no guests; a hosted instance has them, and `me()` answers isOwner and canEdit from env.token alone, so a hosted guest reads as a member and a member with publish rights as unable to edit. The server enforces the rights, so a page cannot gain anything by it, but a page that trusts these fields misbehaves.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"755f77437e4c357f9c227a909b248314d87a2588d394fbdfe8c65d3a5fbd33f8"},"suggested_fix":"Carry the hosted viewer's guest flag and rights in CapEnv.viewer and answer from them.","summary":"The user capability tells pages guest: false and computes isOwner and canEdit from the shell token, which is wrong on a hosted instance","tags":["hosted","web","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:57:35.253381Z","id":"9162c0608462d43778b15112aad4c10933760324f21c0cc4c36a859eb51bf1b9","body":{"detail":"addPageComment builds `new ApiError(res.status, msg)` with no code, while `mapped` (web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:136-148) turns a 403 into the transient `unavailable` only when `e.code === \"spectator\"` (the daemon's SPECTATOR_CODE, crates/clax-core/src/seats.rs:51). createThread, sendToAgent and the other thread helpers go through `ok` in web/shell/src/threads.ts:51-59, which keeps `error.code`, so `create` maps the same refusal correctly and `reply` does not. The `seated()` check up front covers a view that already knows it is a spectator, but a seat lost between that check and the POST (the seat pool is the daemon's) reaches `mapped` with code null and is reported as a permanent `forbidden`, telling the page the viewer may never reply. addPageComment also duplicates `ok`'s body otherwise.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":598},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"13eec3cb0933daaae46aece6e47bcda0f5dab22726fe34c31b575ad61effe84c"},"suggested_fix":"Move addPageComment into web/shell/src/threads.ts beside addComment and have it return through `ok` (or parse `error.code` and pass it as ApiError's third argument), so every page write maps refusals by the daemon's code.","summary":"A page's comments.reply drops the daemon's error code, so a spectator's refused reply rejects 'forbidden' instead of 'unavailable'","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:35.988206Z","id":"114118c745a87e1c14f21e7dac3f822c668dce30b3c644118e3ebf056c391eb7","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:605-608 parses only error.message and throws `new ApiError(res.status, msg)`; ApiError's code defaults to null (web/shell/src/api.ts:63). The reply path (comments.ts:355) runs it through request -> mapped (comments.ts:272), and mapped yields `unavailable` only for `e.status === 403 && e.code === \"spectator\"` (comments.ts:142), else `forbidden` (comments.ts:143). threads.ts `ok` (web/shell/src/threads.ts:51-59) does parse error.code. The daemon refuses the comment route with 403 spectator: crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs calls clax_http::seats::require_seat on every thread write route (lines 737, 985, 1242, 1420, 1500, 1642, 1702), which returns spectator_refusal (crates/clax-http/src/seats.rs:67-72, code clax_core::seats::SPECTATOR_CODE). The up-front seated() check (comments.ts:203-205) only covers a view already marked spectating. Kind concern is right: a misclassified error code in a race, not a merge blocker.","kind":"comment","references":"9162c0608462d43778b15112aad4c10933760324f21c0cc4c36a859eb51bf1b9","summary":"confirmed: addPageComment throws ApiError without the daemon's code, so mapped reports a seat lost before a reply as forbidden","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:24:50.505485Z","id":"4f50b36f30a2af57285106804f70a2455881a668cef0caff63f044c3ea9029a2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f309a4046","summary":"Fixed: comments.reply goes through threads.ts addComment(viaPage) and keeps the daemon's error code; caps/comments.test.ts 'a reply the daemon refuses a spectator is unavailable, not forbidden' passes; //web:unit passes.","supersedes":"9162c0608462d43778b15112aad4c10933760324f21c0cc4c36a859eb51bf1b9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
